          ],
          "text": "Roadside inn: a modest two-storey inn of pale limestone blocks on the Jerusalem to Jericho road in Roman Judea, with a flat roof, a low arched gateway wide enough for a laden animal, and an open courtyard with a stone well and a water trough. Scrub and dry terraces of olive and fig stand behind it, and the rough track runs past its gate."
